Z||000000||cscougar||08-28-2001||02:54 PM||||My daughter just called me from College Station, TX.  She took her 86 Fiero by there to have 1 can of R12 Freon added to the AC.  The idiot there wanted $69.95 for the can and another $35.00 to check for leaks.  To top it off, he said that Advance Auto did not work on Fieros because they are too hard to work on.<P>I bet he has never added freon to a car at all if he thinks that is hard to do on a Fiero.  I would do it but she is 100 miles away.<P>Anyone in the Bryan-College Station, TX area know of a good shop for Fieros.<P>Thanks<P>Ted||||reg||1
Z||000001||Spektrum-87GT||08-28-2001||02:58 PM||||ive gotta add  my two cents about advanced. they charged me 20 bucks for a hose. well, it was a power steering hose, and they told me it came with the metal connectors. it took them over a week to get it and it ended up being a 10 inch rubber hose. i've never gone back, never will go back. pep girls isnt much better.<P>to clear things up, it was for my 91 cherokee, definitly not the fiero  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><p>[This message has been edited by Spektrum-87GT (edited 08-28-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||Hank is Here||08-28-2001||07:40 PM||||Maybe I am confused here.  Anyone cannot just buy a can of R12, at least I think.  The 134A stuff that is currently sold in cans does not mix w/ the old R12.   The pice sounds normal for hte old R12 stuff, but steep for 134A.<P>Advance around here is good if you KNOW what you need.  I lie to them all the time on types and years of vehicles, to get the right stuff.  Actually they aren't bad for looking up Fiero stuff but the older stuff they suck at!  I get parts for my dad's 46' Chevy  with 216 by telling them it is a mid 60's pickup with 292 or something like that.  They look at me funny, find the part then I tell them what it IS for after I have the correct part in my hand. lol||||reg||1
